            <ArticleTitle>[Reactive polyarthritis and painful dermatographism caused by Helicobacter pylori].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-102</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes a 36 year-old white woman with six month history of epigastric abdominal pain, reactive arthritis and painful dermographism. Serum antibodies to Helicobacter pylori were identified. All symptoms subsided when she received eradication treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
